restricted licensed lounges and cafes\".\n- **What it rules out:** it treats adult use as legal, so it rules out rungs 1–3 (fully illegal, medical-only, decriminalized possession with no legal sales).\n- **Why no chair:** it never mentions a taxed market, which rung 4 needs, or \"minimal restrictions\", which rung 5 needs. So it can't separate rung 4 from rung 5.\n- **How I coded the passage:** `statement-other`, because the page is about nightlife and permits, not a cannabis issue page.\n- **Other passages:** the Operation Zero Waste page only mentions cannabis-tax funding as an example of nonprofit spending, so I coded it `off`. None of the other sources mention cannabis, so I left them out of the row.\n- **`needs_source`:** his own words on how cannabis should be regulated, such as a debate answer, questionnaire or issue page.\n- **Quote:** I tiered the lounge-permit sentence `lever`, `lever-named`, and marked it quotable.\n\nThe file is `labels/coder-1.json` in the `2026-10-07-shadow-hilton-cannabis-policy` folder.","ttft_ms":12536,"type":"result","duration_ms":31134,"uuid":"c9bbb07e-b9f6-4fa3-a103-17c4651850a4","ttft_stream_ms":1315,"time_to_request_ms":102,"first_content_frame_ms":1316,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
